# Visual brainstorming companion session files
.superpowers/

# Generated data artifacts. data/raw/ is deliberately NOT ignored: the DILIrank
# workbook is 110KB of US-government public-domain data, and committing it pins
# the exact dataset version a result was produced from. DILIrank 2.0 reclassified
# 49 drugs from 1.0, so "which version" is part of the result.
# `data/out/*` and not `data/out/` on purpose: git cannot re-include a file whose
# PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, so the trailing-slash form would make the two
# negations below silently dead.
data/out/*

# Two deliberate exceptions, on the same reasoning that keeps data/raw/ tracked.
#
# spike-report*.json is the record of Task 1's decision gate - the measurement
# that licensed continuing with the conflict-subset thesis. A gate result that
# only ever existed on one machine is not a gate result.
#
# smiles-cache.json pins PubChem's name -> SMILES resolution, which is an input
# to every QSAR number downstream. PubChem is a live service: it can re-resolve a
# name or change a canonicalisation, and then a "reproduction" would silently be
# a different experiment. 94KB to make the resolution part of the provenance.
!data/out/spike-report*.json
!data/out/smiles-cache.json

# compounds.json and splits.json are NOT incidental build output.
#
# The validity of every reported number rests on the three-way split having been
# fixed BEFORE any model was fitted (spec section 8). That is only a real claim if
# the split artifact is in git history with a timestamp earlier than the first
# fitting commit. Left ignored, `git add data/out/splits.json` adds nothing, no
# error is printed, and the strongest methodological claim in the project quietly
# becomes unverifiable.
!data/out/compounds.json
!data/out/splits.json

# The evidence streams themselves: the inputs every reported number is computed
# from. Same reasoning as the split - a benchmark whose inputs exist on one
# machine is not reproducible.
!data/out/stream-*.json
!data/out/evidence.json
!data/out/tak994.json
!data/out/cid-cache.json

# The re-pulled Tox21 tested concentrations (Task 4): a live PubChem pull keyed
# to the AIDs pinned in stream-tox21.json. Same reproducibility reasoning as the
# streams above - the margin Task 5 computes from this is only re-derivable if
# the numbers it was computed from are in git, not just on the machine that ran
# the pull.
!data/out/tox21-concentrations.json

# results/results.json IS the deliverable, not build output: it is the artifact a
# reviewer re-derives the reported numbers from. 676KB.
results/*
!results/results.json
!results/metrics.json
!results/verdict-manifest.json
!results/golden/
!results/golden/metrics.golden.json
# The v2.0 re-grade. Tracked for the same reason results.json is: it is the
# artifact behind the claim that the 0.750 headline was an artifact, and a
# reviewer has to be able to read it without re-running anything.
!results/rescore-v2.txt

# The consistency probe's raw runs. A reported flip rate whose underlying answers
# were discarded is an assertion rather than a measurement, so a LIVE run belongs
# in git. A STUB run does not - it measures the harness, reports 0% by
# construction, and committing one puts a file in the repo that looks exactly like
# a result. Check `"source": "live"` before adding it.
!results/probe-runs.json

# The ask-surface evaluation and the report built from it. Same reasoning as
# results.json: the artifact a reviewer re-derives the reported numbers from, and a
# PDF whose inputs exist on one machine is a claim rather than a measurement. The
# extraction and vector caches under results/library/ stay ignored - those are derived
# from PDFs that are not committed either.
!results/retrieval-eval.json
!results/ask-eval.json
!results/report/
!results/report/arbiter-evaluation.pdf

# Playwright output. The e2e run's traces and screenshots are diagnostics for a
# single run, not artifacts anyone re-derives a number from.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
# Vite's dev-server dependency cache. Written by `npm run web:dev`, not an input to
# anything - `.vite/` and not `apps/web/.vite/` so it is ignored wherever it appears.
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.local
# The hand-out copy. `.env.example` is the tracked template and holds no secret;
# this one carries a live service-account key once section 1 is filled in, which
# is the whole reason it exists as a separate file rather than as an edit to the
# template.
.env.share

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# LibreOffice / Office transient lock files
.~lock.*#
~$*

# Regulatory review PDFs. TRACKED as of 2026-08-16, reversing the earlier decision.
#
# The old rule said they were retrievable from accessdata.fda.gov or ema.europa.eu by
# the URL the spec records. In practice no URL is recorded anywhere - library-sources.json
# names filenames and an NDA number, and there is no fetch script - so "retrievable"
# meant a person hand-searching FDA's site for 35 documents. What a fresh clone actually
# got was a Library where every entry read "cannot be searched: not in this checkout",
# which is the product's central surface failing for a reason that looks like a bug.
#
# 363 MB, and that cost is accepted deliberately: the Ask surface is the thing being
# demonstrated, and a demonstration nobody else can run is not one. Revisit with Git LFS
# if the repository becomes unwieldy - the files are static, so LFS would fit them well.
#
# data/prep/split_review.py still refuses anything it cannot split, so a missing source
# still cannot silently become a hand-trimmed one.

# The DILIrank workbook was downloaded a second time into documents/. It is
# byte-identical to the tracked data/raw/dilirank.xlsx (sha256 1ca1352ff727af68...),
# and two copies of a pinned dataset is how "which version produced this result"
# stops having one answer. The tracked copy is the one under data/raw.
documents/

# Uploaded documents and the account store. Both are runtime state that belongs to
# whoever runs the service, and the account file holds password hashes - a repo is
# not where those live, even scrypted, even for a demo team.
results/documents/
*.users.json

# Atmosphere screenshot output (tuning artefacts, not source)
apps/atmosphere/shots/
apps/landing/shots/

# Worktrees created by the harness. Not part of the repository.
.claude/worktrees/
